„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRSo all the men of Israel were gathered against the city, knit together as one man.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|And the tribes of Israel sent men through all the tribe of Benjamin, saying, What wickedness is this that is done among you?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙòNow therefore deliver us the men, the children of Belial, which are in Gibeah, that we may put them to death, and put away evil from Israel. But the children of Benjamin would not hearken to the voice of their brethren the children of Israel:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒbut the children of Benjamin gathered themselves together out of the cities unto Gibeah, to go out to battle against the children of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÆAnd the children of Benjamin were numbered at that time out of the cities twenty and six thousand men that drew sword, beside the inhabitants of Gibeah, which were numbered seven hundred chosen men.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„Among all this people there were seven hundred chosen men lefthanded; every one could sling stones at an hair breadth, and not miss.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And the men of Israel, beside Benjamin, were numbered four hundred thousand men that drew sword: all these were men of war.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙàAnd the children of Israel arose, and went up to the house of God, and asked counsel of God, and said, Which of us shall go up first to the battle against the children of Benjamin? And the LORD said, Judah shall go up first.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOAnd the children of Israel rose up in the morning, and encamped against Gibeah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰And the men of Israel went out to battle against Benjamin; and the men of Israel put themselves in array to fight against them at Gibeah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd the children of Benjamin came forth out of Gibeah, and destroyed down to the ground of the Israelites that day twenty and two thousand men.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšAnd the people the men of Israel encouraged themselves, and set their battle again in array in the place where they put themselves in array the first day.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙá(And the children of Israel went up and wept before the LORD until even, and asked counsel of the LORD, saying, Shall I go up again to battle against the children of Benjamin my brother? And the LORD said, Go up against him.)¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd the children of Israel came near against the children of Benjamin the second day.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´And Benjamin went forth against them out of Gibeah the second day, and destroyed down to the ground of the children of Israel again eighteen thousand men; all these drew the sword.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙçThen all the children of Israel, and all the people, went up, and came unto the house of God, and wept, and sat there before the LORD, and fasted that day until even, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd the children of Israel enquired of the LORD, (for the ark of the covenant of God was there in those days,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ
and Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron, stood before it in those days,) saying, Shall I yet again go out to battle against the children of Benjamin my brother, or shall I cease? And the LORD said, Go up; for to morrow I will deliver them into thine hand.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse#¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ0And Israel set liers in wait round about Gibeah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”And the children of Israel went up against the children of Benjamin on the third day, and put themselves in array against Gibeah, as at other times.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd the children of Benjamin went out against the people, and were drawn away from the city; and they began to smite of the people, and kill, as at other times, in the highways, of which one goeth up to the house of God, and the other to Gibeah in the field, about thirty men of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ±And the children of Benjamin said, They are smitten down before us, as at the first. But the children of Israel said, Let us flee, and draw them from the city unto the highways.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃAnd all the men of Israel rose up out of their place, and put themselves in array at Baal-tamar: and the liers in wait of Israel came forth out of their places, even out of the meadows of Gibeah.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd there came against Gibeah ten thousand chosen men out of all Israel, and the battle was sore: but they knew not that evil was near them.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ±And the LORD smote Benjamin before Israel: and the children of Israel destroyed of the Benjamites that day twenty and five thousand and an hundred men: all these drew the sword.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse.¦verses›„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹So the children of Benjamin saw that they were smitten: for the men of Israel gave place to the Benjamites, because they trusted unto the liers in wait which they had set beside Gibeah.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•And the liers in wait hasted, and rushed upon Gibeah; and the liers in wait drew themselves along, and smote all the city with the edge of the sword.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜Now there was an appointed sign between the men of Israel and the liers in wait, that they should make a great flame with smoke rise up out of the city.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÌAnd when the men of Israel retired in the battle, Benjamin began to smite and kill of the men of Israel about thirty persons: for they said, Surely they are smitten down before us, as in the first battle.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©But when the flame began to arise up out of the city with a pillar of smoke, the Benjamites looked behind them, and, behold, the flame of the city ascended up to heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtAnd when the men of Israel turned again, the men of Benjamin were amazed: for they saw that evil was come upon them.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃTherefore they turned their backs before the men of Israel unto the way of the wilderness; but the battle overtook them; and them which came out of the cities they destroyed in the midst of them.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Thus they inclosed the Benjamites round about, and chased them, and trode them down with ease over against Gibeah toward the sunrising.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOAnd there fell of Benjamin eighteen thousand men; all these were men of valour.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎAnd they turned and fled toward the wilderness unto the rock of Rimmon: and they gleaned of them in the highways five thousand men; and pursued hard after them unto Gidom, and slew two thousand men of them.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€So that all which fell that day of Benjamin were twenty and five thousand men that drew the sword; all these were men of valour.¦layout ªlast_verse.…¤book§chapter«first_verse/ªlast_verse0¦verses’„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuBut six hundred men turned and fled to the wilderness unto the rock Rimmon, and abode in the rock Rimmon four months.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙìAnd the men of Israel turned again upon the children of Benjamin, and smote them with the edge of the sword, as well the men of every city, as the beast, and all that came to hand: also they set on fire all the cities that they came to.¦layout ªlast_verse0